      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GLENN'S LEGACY (7) broke his maiden nicely at Moruya before being poorly placed in city company last time out. This suits him much better today and he should get all the favours from the barrier. Can bounce back to winning ways in a more suitable assignment. PEACE BIRD (3) shed the maiden tag last start after knocking on the door in provincial grade. Things look to shape similarly for her here, with the rise in trip being no issue. Can find the front again and be tough to run down. LONDON BOY (2) is racing well without winning of late, placing again last start on the Acton at Canberra. Jay Ford replaces the apprentice hoop and he should get every chance from the barrier. Ticks plenty of boxes and can be in the finish yet again. KENDALIA (1) gets the blinkers on for the first time today and is not to be discounted out in trip.",
